# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles are only ever executed inside Linux
# containers - a CRLF checkout (Windows' git default, core.autocrlf=true)
# corrupts a script's "#!/bin/sh" shebang into "#!/bin/sh\r", which the
# kernel can't resolve as an interpreter, so the container fails outright
# with "exec <script>: no such file or directory" instead of starting.
# Force LF regardless of the cloning machine's OS/git config.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
